 #edb/ref 17592186410948 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410990 1079 #uuid "9998cffe-b044-5c0e-8d8d-808f7ebe4f34" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410956 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410963 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410977 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410979 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410983 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1077 "selection" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1078 #edb/ref 17592186410979 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410991 1079 #uuid "f6c39c5e-8a07-5782-972e-e1ea5abb9373" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410992 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410987 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410992 1069 "q-103265" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410992 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410992 1071 "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $55u+24v=\\text{gcd}(55,24).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410992 1072 #uuid "2c3ce546-4615-54b8-9d08-ac0c684680c7" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410992 1074 "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}55 & = & 24\\cdot 2 & + & 7 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 24 & = & 7\\cdot 3 & + & 3 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 7 & = & 3\\cdot 2 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(55,24)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =55-24\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & =24-7\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1 & =7-3\\cdot 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =7-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =7-[24-7\\cdot 3]\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =7\\cdot 7-24\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =[55-24\\cdot 2]\\cdot 7-24\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =55\\cdot 7-24\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =55\\cdot 7+24\\cdot (-16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=7$ and $v=-16.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=7+(-16)=-9.\n$$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410993 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410989 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410993 1069 "q-103236" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410993 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410993 1071 "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $80u+35v=\\text{gcd}(80,35).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410993 1072 #uuid "321cfd56-0a7b-5b4f-978f-55f6493e6553" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410993 1074 "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}80 & = & 35\\cdot 2 & + & 10 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 35 & = & 10\\cdot 3 & + & 5 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 10 & = & 5\\cdot 2 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(80,35)=5.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =80-35\\cdot 2 \\\\ 5 & =35-10\\cdot 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =35-10\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =35-[80-35\\cdot 2]\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =35\\cdot 7-80\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =80\\cdot (-3)+35\\cdot 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-3$ and $v=7.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-3)+7=4.\n$$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410994 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410988 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410994 1069 "q-103258" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410994 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410994 1071 "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $71u+29v=\\text{gcd}(71,29).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410994 1072 #uuid "32ff23bf-0d8e-550e-a2d3-333ad056d2c6" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410994 1074 "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}71 & = & 29\\cdot 2 & + & 13 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 29 & = & 13\\cdot 2 & + & 3 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 13 & = & 3\\cdot 4 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(71,29)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =71-29\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & =29-13\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1 & =13-3\\cdot 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =13-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =13-[29-13\\cdot 2]\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =13\\cdot 9-29\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =[71-29\\cdot 2]\\cdot 9-29\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =71\\cdot 9-29\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =71\\cdot 9+29\\cdot (-22)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=9$ and $v=-22.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=9+(-22)=-13.\n$$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410995 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410984 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410995 1069 "q-79902" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410995 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410995 1071 "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $79u+35v=\\text{gcd}(79,35).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410995 1072 #uuid "5854fb1f-195a-5978-bfc0-db75a9114381" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410995 1074 "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}79 & = & 35\\cdot 2 & + & 9 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 35 & = & 9\\cdot 3 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 9 & = & 8\\cdot 1 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(79,35)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =79-35\\cdot 2 \\\\ 8 & =35-9\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1 & =9-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =9-8 \\\\  & =9-[35-9\\cdot 3] \\\\  & =9\\cdot 4-35 \\\\  & =[79-35\\cdot 2]\\cdot 4-35 \\\\  & =79\\cdot 4-35\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =79\\cdot 4+35\\cdot (-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=4$ and $v=-9.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=4+(-9)=-5.\n$$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410996 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410986 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410996 1069 "q-79848" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410996 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410996 1071 "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $64u+28v=\\text{gcd}(64,28).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410996 1072 #uuid "ef7dfe31-fa62-51d2-b435-2d5f9267bf87" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410996 1074 "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}64 & = & 28\\cdot 2 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 28 & = & 8\\cdot 3 & + & 4 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 8 & = & 4\\cdot 2 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(64,28)=4.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =64-28\\cdot 2 \\\\ 4 & =28-8\\cdot 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =28-8\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =28-(64-28\\cdot 2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =28\\cdot 7-64\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =64\\cdot (-3)+28\\cdot 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-3$ and $v=7.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-3)+7=4.\n$$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410997 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410990 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410997 1069 "q-79901" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410997 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410997 1071 "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $70u+31v=\\text{gcd}(70,31).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410997 1072 #uuid "f595bdf1-0020-53f4-bd59-1e7fad6ce48b" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true] [17592186410997 1074 "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}70 & = & 31\\cdot 2 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 31 & = & 8\\cdot 3 & + & 7 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 8 & = & 7\\cdot 1 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(70,31)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =70-31\\cdot 2 \\\\ 7 & =31-8\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1 & =8-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =8-7 \\\\  & =8-[31-8\\cdot 3] \\\\  & =8\\cdot 4-31 \\\\  & =[70-31\\cdot 2]\\cdot 4-31 \\\\  & =70\\cdot 4-31\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =70\\cdot 4+31\\cdot (-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=4$ and $v=-9.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=4+(-9)=-5.\n$$" 13194139534124 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-020f98df-ce27-5f83-a183-d790fdb0efb4" 17592186410944 "answer-025792a9-1418-5ed0-bd75-63fdf48048ad" 17592186410945 "answer-047f5cfa-c319-5769-a5d9-38ab5eac2e3f" 17592186410946 "answer-130c9d5f-a494-5201-9007-5c05a96b42e6" 17592186410947 "answer-26070e7e-e2f2-538f-a981-409b7228a780" 17592186410948 "answer-2709c658-cd3e-5e8b-b07f-16cf2388e15a" 17592186410949 "answer-3132dcdb-547b-5f5a-85ac-f3d9b7acfe30" 17592186410950 "answer-363673d5-c3de-5c37-9ff1-f75b214ea273" 17592186410951 "answer-3a7e30f3-8d4f-5e6c-9301-12bd11a35aa4" 17592186410952 "answer-3d4f7dfc-8c4b-5211-9ba9-17a6891ea4ab" 17592186410953 "answer-4844b534-18e6-52ed-9d01-29f0d3eda197" 17592186410954 "answer-5e46fd5a-2cae-5e32-9a58-53a8ac056701" 175